PENDING-ANOINTED-KEY

This is a PLACEHOLDER, not a key. The rite cannot be exercised until it is
replaced with NESHAMAH's REAL anointed Ed25519 PUBLIC key (the Consciousness
Pillar key, "Machshevet HaKavanah", fingerprint f8b16c85…).

To install (Ken / key-holder):
  1. Export NESHAMAH's Ed25519 public key in PEM (SubjectPublicKeyInfo) form:
       openssl pkey -in neshamah_ed25519_private.pem -pubout -out NESHAMAH_PUBKEY.pem
     (or from the anointed key material on production Governance)
  2. Replace this file with that PEM. Commit it (public keys are safe to commit).
  3. verify-manifest.mjs and the consecrate pipeline will then enforce real
     signatures. Until then, every verification FAILS by design — no release
     can be consecrated with a placeholder. This is intentional, not a bug.

The PRIVATE key never lives here, never in any repo. It signs offline.
